      <Pad Id="BPzHhcQ1biKMGhdzDxg27U" Bounds="100,0,300,51" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="3. The node. It creates the model and caches it, so the model only changes when a parameter changes.">
        <p:TypeAnnotation>
          <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
        </p:TypeAnnotation>
        <p:ValueBoxSettings>
          <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
        </p:ValueBoxSettings>
      </Pad>
      <Pad Id="L11lppohrnVOkpbE7siJ89" Bounds="100,290,300,51" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="The time boxed model holds the parameters and creates the transition once a preset gets triggered.">
        <p:TypeAnnotation>
          <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
        </p:TypeAnnotation>
        <p:ValueBoxSettings>
          <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
        </p:ValueBoxSettings>
      </Pad>
      <Pad Id="UMWjXmYHFSJMUZv1mVDtjx" Bounds="100,130,300,85" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1. The model. It doesn't know the duration yet: a transition gets triggered with a duration, which is why the model hands out a &quot;time boxed&quot; version of itself when asked for a given duration.">
        <p:TypeAnnotation>
          <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
        </p:TypeAnnotation>
        <p:ValueBoxSettings>
          <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
        </p:ValueBoxSettings>
      </Pad>
      <Pad Id="MT1tGooSEugN7VHeFyzzeb" Bounds="100,580,300,34" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Where the presets of this patch are stored.">
        <p:TypeAnnotation>
          <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
        </p:TypeAnnotation>
        <p:ValueBoxSettings>
          <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
        </p:ValueBoxSettings>
      </Pad>
      <Pad Id="Ia3Wo1ZIh6CPkYxCnzNq6b" Bounds="100,420,300,85" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="2. The transition. The runtime asks it every frame: Update (is it still running?) and Compute (what is the value now?). When Update says it is done, the runtime writes the final value to the channel.">
        <p:TypeAnnotation>
          <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
        </p:TypeAnnotation>
        <p:ValueBoxSettings>
          <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
        </p:ValueBoxSettings>
      </Pad>
    </Canvas>
